<title>RUSSIA: AGROKHLEB-Russian '97 beet sowing seen at '96 levels.</title>
<headline>AGROKHLEB-Russian '97 beet sowing seen at '96 levels.</headline>
<text>
<p>The following is a direct contribution from SovEcon Ltd, an independent research organisation specialising in agricultural production and trade in the former Soviet Union.</p>
<p>RUSSIA: SUGARBEET AREA IN 1997 EXPECTED TO MATCH 1996 LEVELS</p>
<p>MOSCOW, May 12 - Russia's total area sown to sugarbeet this season is expected to be around last year's level of 1.1 million hectares, assuming a normal development for the sowing campaign.</p>
<p>Sugarbeet sowings had started in most producing areas as at the beginning of May, and the total area sown to sugarbeet is close to normal levels for this time of year.</p>
<p>Cold weather in April means sugarbeet sowings in North Caucasus are lagging behind normal. But sugarbeet sowings in Central-Chernozem (Black Earth) region, Russia's main sugarbeet producing area, are slightly above average, particularly in the Voronezh Oblast (Province).</p>
